;; The known non-passes of bin/cppi lower-check (doc/cpp/LLVM.md §9; doc/cpp/CPP-SURVEY.md, "As built: CX6 (write-ahead)"): a
;; file of a check list -> its class. Read with the Clojure reader. The classes:
;;   :library-throw   the program catches an exception that the shared libstdc++ throws (std::__throw_*, basic_ios::clear,
;;                    use_facet's bad_cast): it unwinds natively through the lowered C, which has no landing pads (§8);
;;                    gone when CX7 lowers libstdc++ with the program
;;   :callback-throw  a virtual function of the program (a streambuf's overflow, sync, underflow) throws while libstdc++'s
;;                    code calls it: the pending flag returns into native frames that do not test it (§8); the same remedy
;;   :exception-ptr   std::exception_ptr, std::current_exception, std::rethrow_exception, std::make_exception_ptr: the
;;                    lowering refuses them until the runtime of CX7 holds libsupc++'s exception objects
